5. PLATFORM PERMISSIONS (GITHUB)

This repository is hosted on GitHub and is intentionally public (among other
reasons, the in-app updater relies on its public releases). Under the GitHub
Terms of Service (section D.5, "License Grant to Other Users"), making a
repository public grants other GitHub users a nonexclusive, worldwide license
to use, display, perform and reproduce (by forking) its content "through the
Service as permitted by GitHub's functionality". This License does not and
cannot remove those platform permissions.

This License grants nothing beyond them. A fork on GitHub is a copy within
the GitHub service; it does not authorize anyone to build, modify,
redistribute, publish or commercially exploit Cyclo, or any part of it,
outside what Sections 3 and 4 allow. Content uploaded to GitHub is also
subject to the rights GitHub obtains under its own Terms of Service, which
are a matter between each user and GitHub.


